# CongaTimeout Property

Applies to:{.prefix}

Server{.info}

The CongaTimeout property specifies the number of milliseconds at which the Conga wait should
timeout and the server should perform housekeeping. The default value is 5000 (5 seconds).

On a busy server the Conga wait may never time out, because every event starts it again. The
server therefore also performs housekeeping when an event arrives and CongaTimeout milliseconds
have passed since housekeeping last ran. CongaTimeout is in effect the housekeeping interval.

At each housekeeping, in addition to Rumba's built-in housekeeping, Rumba executes the
→[OnCongaTimeout] callback. This function may do additional, application specific housekeeping.

